From: =?UTF-8?q?Ant=C3=B3nio=20Sarmento?= <Keyaku@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 12:42:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] SurfaceFlinger: force client composition for an independent
 external display

The 8.1 MTK composer demotes external-display layers to client composition
but does not report the change to SurfaceFlinger, so SF never renders a
client target and the external session starves. Force SF to client-compose
when the external is showing its own layer stack rather than mirroring the
primary. This is part of the HDMI Presentation work; the blob-side half is
still being iterated.

Changes:
- CompositionEngine/src/Display.cpp: after deriveCompositionType, override an independent external to client composition

Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Ieeb9029131f739f9d7d28924869e11bcd961748c
---
 .../surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/Display.cpp | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/Display.cpp b/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/Display.cpp
index 3b21ab0b21..da6dbaa830 100644
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/Display.cpp
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/CompositionEngine/src/Display.cpp
@@ -273,6 +273,18 @@ void Display::chooseCompositionStrategy() {
         state.usesClientComposition = false;
         state.usesDeviceComposition = true;
     }
+
+    // The 8.1 MTK composer demotes an external display's own layers to client
+    // composition but does not report the change back to SurfaceFlinger, so SF
+    // never renders a client target and the external session starves. Force SF
+    // to client-compose an external display that is not mirroring the primary.
+    if (!isExternalMirrorStack() && mId && !state.usesClientComposition) {
+        const auto& hwc = getCompositionEngine().getHwComposer();
+        if (hwc.getDisplayConnectionType(*mId) == android::DisplayConnectionType::External) {
+            state.usesClientComposition = true;
+            state.usesDeviceComposition = false;
+        }
+    }
 }
 
 bool Display::isExternalMirrorStack() const {
